 "final_text": "All fields submitted. Here's the summary:\n\n---\n\n**Run committed: PR-00001** \u2014 four CONTRACT vendor invoices due 2026-03-13, paid from USMF-OPER.\n\n| Invoice | Vendor | Gross | Withholding | Net |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| WINV-801 | Granite State Engineering (WVEN-01) | $50,000 | $0 | $50,000 |\n| WINV-802 | Juniper Field Services (WVEN-02) | $30,000 | $7,200 (24%) | $22,800 |\n| WINV-803 | Meridian Analytics Ltd (WVEN-03) | $40,000 | $12,000 (30%) | $28,000 |\n| WINV-804 | Nordwind Design GmbH (WVEN-04) | $20,000 | $3,000 (15%) | $17,000 |\n| **Totals** | | **$140,000** | **$22,200** | **$117,800** |\n\n**Key decisions per SOP-AP-09:**\n\n- **WVEN-02 (Juniper):** Tax category \"none\" but no W-9 on file \u2192 punitive default: backup withholding at **24%**.\n- **WVEN-03 (Meridian):** W-8BEN-E expired 2025-12-31. Their email claiming 15% treaty rate is not a certificate \u2014 per SOP-AP-09, a lapsed certificate is not a certificate. Applied the punitive foreign-contractor rate of **30%** (not the 15% they asked for).\n- **WVEN-04 (Nordwind):** Valid W-8BEN-E through 2027-12-31 \u2192 treaty rate **15%**.\n- **WVEN-01 (Granite State):** Domestic corp, W-9 on file \u2192 no withholding.",
